Social, cultural, and intellectual history (@social-cultural-and-intellectual-history: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_6KTBZD5S9MQP7X644VN1AXS90B
This material examines how people lived, worked, thought, believed, communicated, and organised their relationships across time. It connects everyday practices, class, family, gender, religion, education, cultural production, and the circulation of ideas with their material settings and surviving evidence. Routes can follow a practice, concept, group, or work through several contexts, linking broad historical accounts to particular lives. Share sources with Sociology, Philosophy, and Literature while explaining the limits of treating a text or example as representative of an entire society.

**Parent:** [History](../History.lingua#r_3MKG6XS2X0W9YR8T4438CTGZ1T).
